    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0807" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg707"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/823a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-13T18:00:00-04:00">September 13, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. We have today completed an exchange of notes with the Spanish Government
                    giving reciprocal assurances regarding a fair share of quotas as outlined to you
                    in our 43, Aug. 21, 5 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d596-f1"/></p>
                <p>We are accordingly prepared to give public notice in the press appearing Monday
                    evening, September 17, of intention to negotiate a <pb facs="0808" n="708"
                        xml:id="pg708"/> foreign trade agreement with the Government of
                        Spain.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d596-f2"/> Announcement will be made at the
                    same time for the benefit of American interests concerned, that the Committee
                    for Reciprocity Information has prescribed that all information and views in
                    writing and all applications for supplemental oral presentation of views shall
                    be submitted to the Chairman not later than November 5; oral presentation of
                    views by persons whose applications therefor have been approved will be heard
                    November 12.</p>
                <p>Please inform Spanish Government in case it desires to make simultaneous
                    announcement and report, if possible, by Saturday whether this course is
                    agreeable to the Spanish Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
